  "corrections": [
    "elec-components.md: Ordinary diode symbols have no current-direction arrow.",
    "elec-ohms-law.md: Correct diode and LED symbol interpretation.",
    "elec-ohms-law.md: Chassis and circuit ground need not be directly bonded.",
    "elec-ohms-law.md: Original universal rule contradicts galvanic isolation.",
    "elec-ohms-law.md: Scope the ground rule.",
    "elec-noise-grounding.md: Mixed-signal layout cannot be reduced to mandatory split grounds.",
    "elec-noise-grounding.md: Multi-point/common-plane connections can be the correct design.",
    "elec-noise-grounding.md: Keep takeaway consistent.",
    "elec-noise-grounding.md: Add authoritative grounding reference.",
    "elec-ohms-law.questions.json: Correct misleading diode-arrow teaching.",
    "elec-ohms-law.questions.json: Scope shared-ground requirement.",
    "elec-noise-grounding.questions.json: Remove universal star/split-ground rule.",
    "elec-noise-grounding.md: Microvolt noise is not universally audible.",
    "elec-logic-levels.md: Absolute max is a stress limit, not guaranteed survival.",
    "elec-dividers.md: Reference nodes may not drive pot current.",
    "elec-dividers.md: Avoid recommending arbitrary VREF loading.",
    "elec-dividers.questions.json: 5 V times 0.5 is 2.5 V, not over 3.3 V.",
    "elec-components.questions.json: 390 ohms is also about 5 mA; state rounding criterion.",
    "elec-components.questions.json: Nominal 3.9 mA does not guarantee 4 mA limit under tolerances.",
    "elec-measurement-soldering.md: HSE recommends extraction, not a generic fan.",
    "elec-noise-grounding.questions.json: Power-source substitution is not uniquely diagnostic.",
    "retrofit: elec-components.md: E12 formula note said only 27 and 33 deviate from rounding 10^(n/12); the E-series standard's deviating E12 values are 27, 33, 39, 47 and 82 (formula 26.1, 31.6, 38.3, 46.4, 82.5).",
    "retrofit: elec-components.md: 'C0G/NP0 ceramics ... only come in small values' reworded to 'much smaller values than Class 2 types of the same size' (hedge, matches glossary).",
    "retrofit: glossary rectifier-diode: 'rectifying mains supplies draw current twice per cycle' applies to full-wave rectifiers only; now says so.",
    "retrofit: glossary ground-loop-isolator: 'usually a pair of audio transformers' changed to 'an audio transformer in each signal line'.",
    "retrofit: glossary arm-architecture: 'used in most modern microcontrollers' softened to 'many modern 32-bit microcontrollers'.",
    "retrofit: glossary aliases removed because they capture ordinary words or other meanings elsewhere in the app: 'momentary', 'clamping' (DSA/networks clamping), 'inductive' (inductive proofs), 'twisting', 'temperature-controlled', 'recommended range', 'Class 2' (e.g. USB Audio Class 2), 'four-band'/'five-band' (EQ bands), 'split rail(s)' (bipolar supply meaning), 'keyed' (databases), bare 'TS' (TypeScript in languages) replaced by 'TS jack/cable/plug/connection(s)'."
